(ylacombe/google-chilean-spanish); OpenSLR SLR71 declares CC BY-SA 4.0 for its
recordings. Dataset recordings are not bundled. Exact model-source provenance
and redistribution obligations remain part of signed-release review.

The APK uses Kotlin, coroutines, kotlinx.serialization, AndroidX/Compose, Guava ListenableFuture,
JetBrains annotations and JSpecify. Their resolved runtime inputs declare
Apache-2.0 in Maven metadata, including Guava's parent metadata. The reviewed
component/metadata/artifact inventory is bundled in
assets/licenses/android-runtime-components.json. The identical license texts
found in the AndroidX inputs are retained without modification in
assets/licenses/Android-runtime-Apache-2.0.txt. Existing upstream native/model
notices remain separate. See docs/dependencies.md for scope and release review.
Kotlin's standard-library time code includes ThreeTen-derived code under
BSD-3-Clause. Its copyright, conditions and disclaimer are retained in
assets/licenses/Kotlin-stdlib-ThreeTen-BSD-3-Clause.txt. Upstream Kotlin and
coroutines attribution notices are retained in Kotlin-distribution-NOTICE.txt
and Coroutines-NOTICE.txt in that directory. The Kotlin compiler is build tooling;
retaining its upstream distribution attribution does not bundle that compiler.
The app license does not relicense those artifacts.
